  "question": {
    "text": "If the tangents <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math> are drawn from a variable point <math><mi>P</mi></math> to the ellipse <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> such that the fourth point <math><mi>S</mi></math> of the parallelogram <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>R</mi></math> lies on the circumcircle of the&nbsp;<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>, then the area (in sq. units) of the locus of <math><mi>P</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "LsZVu",
      "text": "<math><mn>7</mn><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9OwjV",
      "text": "<math><mn>16</mn><mi>π</mi></math>",
      "image": null,
